# .NET build output, named down to the two output directories rather than all of bin/.
#
# The blanket rule swallowed bin/sync-contracts — the script the comment below names, and the one
# that fetches the contracts this project's .csproj compiles against. `git add` reported success
# and staged nothing, so a fresh clone had no way to produce .contracts/ and the build failed at
# a <Protobuf Include=".contracts/proto/..."> that pointed at a directory nothing creates.
**/bin/Debug/
**/bin/Release/
obj/
.vscode/
.idea/
.env
!.env.example

# Wire contracts, fetched by bin/sync-contracts at a pinned commit. Never committed.
/.contracts/
